.TH "HTTPDATE" "8" "version 1.0.0" "httpdate"
.SH "NAME"
httpdate \- Time synchronization via HTTP/HTTPS
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B httpdate
[\-adhDFhsx] [\-p precision] [\-P proxy] [URLs] ...
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Httpdate retrieves the date and time from remote web servers via HTTP or HTTPS. Httpdate works through proxy servers and uses libcurl for secure and robust protocol support.
.P
Accuracy of httpdate depends on network latency and precision settings, typically achieving sub-second to millisecond accuracy. If this is not sufficient for your requirements, consider using the ntpd or chrony package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I \-a
Adjust time gradually (smoothly) using the system clock adjustment interface.
.TP
.I \-d
Turn debug/verbose output on (can be specified multiple times for increased verbosity).
.TP
.I \-D
Run as a daemon for continuous background time synchronization.
.TP
.I \-F
Run the daemon in the foreground (e.g. for systemd).
.TP
.I \-h
Show help information and exit.
.TP
.I \-p precision
Precision specifies the number of bisect operations (1 to 9, default: 3) to find the 'second boundary'. Higher precision increases accuracy.
.TP
.I \-P proxy
Use a proxy server for connections (e.g., http://proxy:port or host:port).
.TP
.I \-s
Set time immediately.
.TP
.I \-v
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.I \-x
Adjust time and clock frequency (drift correction), designed for continuous operation in daemon mode (`-D`).
.TP
.I URL
Path to resource or web server endpoint, e.g., https://pool.ntp.org or https://time.google.com
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
Httpdate supports standard proxy environment variables for HTTP(S) connections:
.IP "\fBhttp_proxy\fR" 4
.IX Item "http_proxy"
.PD
If set, the http_proxy variable should contain the URL of the proxy for HTTP connections.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Request time from multiple web servers without modifying the local clock:
.br
\&    httpdate example.com http://example.com https://example.com
.P
Run as daemon mode in the foreground with drift correction (e.g. for systemd):
.br
\&    httpdate \-F \-x https://example.com
.P
Debug/verbose output:
.br
\&    httpdate \-d \-d example.com
.P
Set time immediately:
.br
\&    httpdate \-s example.com
.P
.SH "AUTHOR"
Eddy Vervest
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR htpdate,
.BR rdate,
.BR timed,
.BR ntpd,
.BR systemd
